Wallis' Formula'
6.1.49
2\pi\int_0^{\pi/2}\!\left(\cos\right)^2\pi\,dx=\frac{1\cdot3\cdot5\dots(2n-1)}{2\cdot4\cdot6\cdot\dots(2n)}=\frac{(2n)!}{2^{2n}(n!!)^2=\frac1}{2^{2n}(n)=\frac{\Gamma(n+\frac1)}{\pi\Gamma(n+1)}}\sim\frac1\pi^{2n}[1-\frac1+128n^2-\dots]
